t prey, empty of toil]"}, {"id": "plouteo-note3", "translation": "where, however, πόνου πλουτοῦντα [being rich in toil] is strangely said, when it could more fittingly be said κενὸν πόνον πονοῦντα [toiling an empty toil], as Pers. 682 τίνα πόλις πονεῖ πόνον; [what toil does the city toil?]; which is Gomperz's conjecture (Sitzungsberichte der K. Akademie der Wissenschaften 1875. Bd. 79, 1. S. 236.)."}, {"id": "plouteo-quote1", "translation": "he sent him rich to the house"}, {"id": "plouteo-word1", "translation": "Never yet has any day made Actaeon without prey, empty of toil"}, {"id": "plouteo-word2", "translation": "being rich in toil"}, {"id": "plouteo-word3", "translation": "toiling an empty toil"}, {"id": "plouteo-word4", "translation": "what toil does the city toil"}, {"id": "ploutizo-orth1", "translation": "to enrich, to make wealthy"}, {"id": "ploutizo-def1", "translation": "to enrich, to make wealthy"}, {"id": "ploutizo-note1", "translation": "Ἄλλην τιν᾿ ἄτην ἀντ᾿ ἐμοῦ [some other ruin in place of me]"}, {"id": "ploutizo-note2", "translation": "where Stanley rightly, as it seems, reads ἄτης [of ruin], since πλουτεῖν [to be rich] is construed with the genitive."}, {"id": "ploutizo-note3", "translation": "Σὺν δὲ [and with]"}, {"id": "ploutizo-note4", "translation": "said by tmesis for συμπλουτίζειν [to enrich together], which see."}, {"id": "ploutizo-quote1", "translation": "you enrich"}, {"id": "ploutizo-quote2", "translation": "to enrich me"}, {"id": "ploutizo-word1", "translation": "some other ruin in place of me"}, {"id": "ploutizo-word2", "translation": "of ruin"}, {"id": "ploutizo-word3", "translation": "to be rich"}, {"id": "ploutizo-word4", "translation": "and with"}, {"id": "ploutizo-word5", "translation": "to enrich together"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-orth1", "translation": "rejoicing in wealth"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-def1", "translation": "rejoicing in wealth"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-note1", "translation": "Doric for πλουτογηθής [rejoicing in wealth]"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-note2", "translation": "Πλουτογαθῆ [rejoicing in wealth]"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-quote1", "translation": "recess"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-word1", "translation": "rejoicing in wealth"}, {"id": "ploutogathes-word2", "translation": "rejoicing in wealth"}, {"id": "ploutos-orth1", "translation": "wealth, riches"}, {"id": "ploutos-def1", "translation": "wealth, riches"}, {"id": "ploutos-note1", "translation": "Τῶν [of the]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note2", "translation": "Ὑπὸ δὲ σώματι γᾶς [and under the body of the earth]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note3", "translation": "Μέγας [great]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note4", "translation": "where Heimsoethius corrected to μέγας δαίμων [great divinity]."}, {"id": "ploutos-note5", "translation": "Ἔστι γὰρ [for there is]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note6", "translation": "Πλοῦτος [Wealth]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note7", "translation": "Πολὺς [much]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note8", "translation": "Πολὺς [much]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note9", "translation": "Μέγαν τέκνοις [great for the children]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note10", "translation": "Τοῖς θανούσι [for the dead]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note11", "translation": "Οὐ γὰρ ἔστιν ἔπαλξις [for there is no defense]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note12", "translation": "Ἀκασκαῖον δ᾽ ἄγαλμα [and an unadorned delight]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note13", "translation": "Δύναμιν οὐ σέβουσα πλούτου [not revering the power of wealth]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note14", "translation": "Σποδός προπέμπει πίονας [ash sends forth the rich]"}, {"id": "ploutos-note15", "translation": "Σωματοφθορεῖν ποσὶν φθείροντα [to destroy the body, destroying with the feet]"}]}